## Test Anti-Pattern Audit: `ProductCatalogTests.cs`

This is a textbook case of **"coverage-farming"** — every production method is exercised but almost nothing is verified. These tests will pass even if the code is completely wrong.

---

### 🔴 CRITICAL — Assertion-Free Tests (Coverage Without Verification)

| # | Test | Problem |
|---|------|---------|
| 1 | `AddProduct_Works` | **Zero assertions.** Would pass even if `Save()` threw silently or did nothing. |
| 2 | `UpdatePrice_Works` | **Zero assertions.** Never checks the price actually changed. A bug where `Save` is never called would pass. |
| 3 | `RemoveProduct_Works` | **Zero assertions.** Never verifies the product is gone. |
| 4 | `GetProductCount_Works` | **Zero assertions.** Doesn't even check the count value. |
| 5 | `ApplyBulkDiscount_Works` | **Zero assertions.** Never verifies prices were reduced. This is the most dangerous — a math bug (e.g., `Price * fraction` instead of `Price * (1-fraction)`) passes undetected. |
| 6 | `ImportFromCsv_Works` | **Zero assertions.** Never checks products were actually imported. |

**Fix pattern:**
```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void AddProduct_StoresProduct()
{
    var product = new Product("SKU-001", "Widget", 9.99m);
    _catalog.AddProduct(product);

    var retrieved = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");
    Assert.AreEqual("Widget", retrieved!.Name);
    Assert.AreEqual(9.99m, retrieved.Price);
}
```

---

### 🟠 HIGH — Shallow/Trivial Assertions (Assert.IsNotNull only)

| # | Test | Problem |
|---|------|---------|
| 7 | `GetProduct_Works` | Asserts `IsNotNull` but never verifies the **correct** product was returned. If `FindBySku` returned the wrong product, this passes. |
| 8 | `SearchProducts_Works` | Asserts the list is not null but never checks it contains the right item or has the correct count. An empty list passes. |
| 9 | `GetAllProducts_Works` | Same — a list of 0 items passes. |
| 10 | `ExportToCsv_Works` | An empty or malformed string passes. |

**Fix pattern:**
```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void GetProduct_ReturnsCorrectProduct()
{
    _catalog.AddProduct(new Product("SKU-001", "Widget", 9.99m));
    var result = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");

    Assert.AreEqual("SKU-001", result!.Sku);
    Assert.AreEqual("Widget", result.Name);
    Assert.AreEqual(9.99m, result.Price);
}

[TestMethod]
public void SearchProducts_ReturnsMatchingItems()
